1", "volume-title": "Nuclear Decay Experiments, and Models of Wave Function Collapse!, Physical,Review Letters, 73", "author": "Pearle P."}, {"key": "p_25", "volume-title": "[197S]: The'Web of Belief", "author": "Quine W. V."}, {"key": "p_26", "first-page": "4404", "volume-title": "Physical Review A,\"S1", "author": "Tessieri L."}, {"key": "p_27", "volume-title": "Mathematische Grundlagen der Quantenmechanik", "author": "Von Neumann J.", "year": "1955"}], "container-title": ["The British Journal for the Philosophy of Science"], "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/pdf/10.1093/bjps/48.3.313", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2020, 12, 18]], "date-time": "2020-12-18T21:14:00Z", "timestamp": 1608326040000}, "score": 60.500603, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/10.1093/bjps/48.3.313"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[1997, 9, 1]]}, "references-count": 20, "journal-issue": {"issue": "3", "published-print": {"date-parts": [[1997, 9, 1]]}}, "alternative-id": ["10.1093/bjps/48.3.313"], "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1093/bjps/48.3.313", "ISSN": ["0007-0882", "1464-3537"], "issn-type": [{"value": "0007-0882", "type": "print"}, {"value": "1464-3537", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[1997, 9, 1]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2025, 11, 4]], "date-time": "2025-11-04T15:36:27Z", "timestamp": 1762270587782}, "reference-count": 11, "publisher": "Cambridge University Press (CUP)", "issue": "5", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 1]], "date-time": "2022-01-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1640995200000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 6606, "URL": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/terms"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Philos. of Sci."], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2003, 12]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>It is widely acknowledged that the link between quantum language and ordinary language must be “fuzzier” than the traditional eigenstate-eigenvalue link. In the context of spontaneous-collapse theories, Albert and Loewer (1996) argue that the form of this fuzzy link is a matter of convention, and can be freely chosen to minimize anomalies for those theories. I defend the position that the form of the link is empirical, and could be such as to render collapse theories idle. This means that defenders of spontaneous-collapse theories must gamble that the actual form of the link renders such theories tenable.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1086/377420", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2004, 2, 25]], "date-time": "2004-02-25T16:31:15Z", "timestamp": 1077726675000}, "page": "1437-1446", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 5, "title": ["Quantum Mechanics and Ordinary Language: The Fuzzy Link"], "prefix": "10.1017", "volume": "70", "author": [{"given": "Peter J.", "family": "Lewis", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "56", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 1]]}, "reference": [{"key": "S0031824800001860_R9", "first-page": "22", "article-title": "What Is It Like to Be Schrödinger's Cat?", "volume": "60", "author": "Lewis", "year": "2000", "journal-title": "What Is It Like to Be Schrödinger's Cat?"}, {"key": "S0031824800001860_R2", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "DOI": "10.4159/9780674020146", "volume-title": "Quantum Mechanics and Experience", "author": "Albert", "year": "1992"}, {"key": "S0031824800001860_R11", "volume-title": "Time's Arrow and Archimedes'Point", "author": "Price", "year": "1996"}, {"key": "S0031824800001860_R7", "first-page": "470", "article-title": "Unified Dynamics for Microscopic and Macroscopic Systems", "volume": "D34", "author": "Ghirardi", "year": "1986", "journal-title": "Unified Dynamics for Microscopic and Macroscopic Systems"}, {"key": 